{{/*
  error — the full-page deck-error shell.

  internal/server serves this page, as the current state of the presentation,
  whenever the watched deck fails validation: exactly one author-facing error,
  the string produced by internal/validate.Format ("file:line › path: what —
  fix"). The terminal prints the identical string, so the author sees one
  message in both places (requirements.requirement.error-reporting,
  requirements.requirement.live-reload-error-page).

  It is a standalone page: OFFLINE, and — unlike the deck and gallery pages —
  it is a built-in embedded shell, not project-theme-styled: it never
  references the project's theme stylesheet, never a CDN or any network
  location (global.constraint.go-static-embedded-binary). Every colour, font
  and spacing value it uses is a neutral custom property defined inline in
  this file's own <style> block, so the page renders correctly with zero
  external CSS dependencies.

  Embedding / access:
    The pages sub-tree is embedded by internal/assets and exposed as
    assets.Pages() (an fs.FS rooted at pages/), so this file's path is
    "error.html.tmpl". internal/server does, in effect:

      template.Must(template.New("error").
          ParseFS(assets.Pages(), "error.html.tmpl"))

    parsing the page in its own template namespace (each page is standalone).

  Execution context (a struct or map[string]any supplying these keys):
    .Title    string   the document <title>. Empty falls back to "eypres".
    .Message  string   the single author-facing error, exactly as
                       validate.Format(verr) rendered it. Shown verbatim and
                       html/template-escaped. Empty falls back to a generic
                       sentence; internal/server always sets it.

  Hook slots:
    "live-reload" is a named block, exactly like the deck page's, so
    internal/server overrides it with {{ define "live-reload" }} before
    parsing and injects its SSE client script there. Because the error page
    carries the same block as deck.html.tmpl, a fixing edit reloads the page
    back to the deck without a manual refresh (live-reload).
*/}}

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ with .Title }}{{ . }}{{ else }}eypres{{ end }}</title>

  {{/* This page is a built-in embedded shell (not project-theme-styled),
       so it never links the project's theme stylesheet. */}}
  <style>
    /* Self-contained: neutral custom properties defined and consumed only
       within this file, so the page renders with zero external CSS
       dependencies. */
    :root {
      --error-space-1: 0.25rem;
      --error-space-2: 0.5rem;
      --error-space-3: 1rem;
      --error-space-4: 1.5rem;
      --error-space-5: 2rem;
      --error-content-width: 90%;
      --error-bg: #1a1a1a;
      --error-fg: #f0f0f0;
      --error-fg-muted: #a0a0a0;
      --error-highlight: #ff6b6b;
      --error-ink-soft: #2a2a2a;
      --error-border-width: 1px;
      --error-radius: 0.375rem;
      --error-font-body: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --error-font-display: var(--error-font-body);
      --error-font-mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", Menlo, monospace;
      --error-font-size-title: 1.75rem;
      --error-font-size-body: 1rem;
      --error-font-size-small: 0.875rem;
      --error-line-height: 1.5;
    }
    html, body { margin: 0; }
    body {
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: var(--error-space-5);
      background: var(--error-bg);
      color: var(--error-fg);
      font-family: var(--error-font-body);
      line-height: var(--error-line-height);
    }
    .error-page { width: var(--error-content-width); max-width: 60rem; }
    .error-page__heading {
      font-family: var(--error-font-display);
      font-size: var(--error-font-size-title);
      margin: var(--error-space-4) 0 var(--error-space-3);
    }
    .error-page__message {
      margin: 0 0 var(--error-space-4);
      padding: var(--error-space-3);
      border: var(--error-border-width) solid var(--error-highlight);
      border-radius: var(--error-radius);
      background: var(--error-ink-soft);
      color: var(--error-highlight);
      font-family: var(--error-font-mono);
      font-size: var(--error-font-size-body);
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    .error-page__hint {
      color: var(--error-fg-muted);
      font-size: var(--error-font-size-small);
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="error-page">
    <h1 class="error-page__heading">Deck error</h1>
    <pre class="error-page__message">{{ with .Message }}{{ . }}{{ else }}The deck could not be loaded.{{ end }}</pre>
    <p class="error-page__hint">Fix the file shown above and save; this page reloads automatically.</p>
  </main>

  {{/* Phase-7 live-reload client script is injected here by internal/server. */}}
  {{ block "live-reload" . }}{{ end }}
</body>
</html>
